      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is fine, but I think you can also do \u0027skvm::UPtr{}\u0027 here which will value-initialize (set things to 0) as opposed to default-initialize (things left in indeterminate value). The \u0027skvm::UPtr{0}\u0027 is C for universal zero (it even works for zero sized structs) and \u0027skvm::UPtr{}\u0027 is more or less the C++ equivalent. Note that these two are treated very differently depending on compiling for C or C++.\n\nIn any event, this is fine and probably a better idea anyway.",
